OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Fri 14 Aug to Sun 23 Aug
OL,6,FSomething of a north to south split to
OL,7,Fstart the period. Some rain or showers
OL,8,Fare likely in the north whilst it will
OL,9,Fbe predominantly dry, sunny and hot in
OL,10,Fthe south. The heat in the south will
OL,11,Flikely ease into next weekend but
OL,12,Fprobably remain a little above
OL,13,Faverage. Further into August, there
OL,14,Fare signs that low pressure systems
OL,15,Fwith spells or rain or thundery
OL,16,Finterludes will interrupt the more
OL,17,Fsettled conditions at times, but
OL,18,Frainfall amounts will probably be
OL,19,Fvariable, with some areas continuing
OL,20,Fto see relatively little. Temperatures
OL,21,Fare likely to remain above average,
OL,22,Fwith a chance of occasional returns of
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fthe hot conditions seen earlier in the
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fperiod.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
